          <transcript>+++ -- abisiγ øgkyi;</transcript>
          <definition> T. mngon par dbang bskur ba; S. abhisheka. Bestowal of spiritual power or consecration. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠪᠣᠳᠠ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- boda; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon sum; S. pratvaksha. Quite evident. ED 374 b. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠪᠣᠯᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- bolxu; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par hbyung ba; S abhinishkramana Leaving_ home to become a monk; name of a a Buddhist sutra portraying the life of Šagjamuni. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠲᠣᠭᠤᠯᠤᠭᠰᠠᠨ ᠪᠤᠷᠬᠠᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- toγuluγsan (burxan) ;</transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par rdzogs par sangs rgyas ; S. abhisambuddha. Fully enlightened (Buddha ). ED 58 b. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠲᠣᠭᠤᠯᠤᠭᠰᠠᠨ ᠪᠣᠳᠢ ᠬᠤᠲᠤᠭ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- toγuluγsan bodi xutuγ; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon parrdzogs par byang chub; S. abhisambodhi.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠭᠠᠷᠬᠤᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- γarxui; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par hbyung ba; S. adbhuta. Miracle, marvel, amazed; also name of a class of Scripture. ED llb. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠮᠠᠭᠲᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- maγtaxu; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par stod pa; S. abhinand-; stotra. To praise worship. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠨᠣᠮ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- nom; </transcript>
          <definition>T. .chos mngon; S. abhidharma. A very controversial term, sometimes transl. improperly by 'metaphysics.' </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠣᠨᠤᠭᠰᠠᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- onuγsan; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par rtogs pa; S. abhisamaya. Realization, full comprehension; also the realization of the deity in the oγtarγui by the bytygelcin. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠰᠠᠨ ᠰᠠᠭᠤᠭᠰᠠᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- san saγuγsan;</transcript>
          <definition> T. mngon sum du bzhugs pa; S. samniukha. Facing toward; having directly in view. ED 571 a - b. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠤᠬᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- uxaxu; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par rtogs pa; S. abhisamaya. Intuitive realization. ED 58 a. </definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠢᠯᠡᠳᠲᠡ ᠬᠤᠷᠢᠶᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ -- xurijaxu; </transcript>
          <definition>T. mngon par bsdu ba; S. abhinirhara. Accomplishment, effectuation; obsequies.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
